"Small Kitchen Appliances You'll Use and Love (I Do!) - Satori Design for Living (https://satoridesignforliving.com/small-kitchen-appliances-youll-use-and-love-i-do/)\nciteturn4view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn2view0\",\"lineno\":10}); Total lines: 110\nL0: Get access to the cite0†MEMBERS ONLY LIBRARY !\nL1: \nL2: cite1†The Recipe Box L3: \nL4: [Input: Search …] [Input]\nL5: \nL6: cite0†SUBSCRIBE!  Get access to the Members Only Library> L7: \nL8: cite2†Breakfast Recipes | cite3†Fab Finds | cite4†Food Love | cite5†Kitchen | cite6†Our Home Projects L9: # Small Kitchen Appliances You’ll Use and Love (I Do!)\nL10: \nL11: Bycite7†Shauna Oberg September 2020November 2023 Updated:November 2023\nL12: \nL13: cite8†0 Comments L14: \nL15: We’re loving the stylish look and handy features of our new smart kettle and toaster from Breville. Bring your kitchen to life with these colourful, intuitive small appliances that seamlessly balance form and function.\nL16: \nL17: cite9†Image: Breville Damson Blue Luxe Kettle in White Kitchen L18: I received products from Breville Canada to facilitate this post. As always, the photos and words are my own. I only partner with brands and products I personally use.\nL19: \nL20: Happy first day of fall! As promised, I’m sharing a few kitchen updates with you today. If your kitchen is feeling a bit bland or tired these days, let me show you how to upgrade the look, feel and function in a matter of minutes! Can we talk about your small kitchen appliances?\nL21: cite10†Image: Blue Breville Toaster on White Kitchen Countertop L22: \nL23: As you may already know, cite11†our kitchen is neutral with varying shades of white in the cabinetry, tile backsplash and quartz countertops, along with stainless steel appliances. Although I’m drawn to light and airy kitchens, ours truly comes alive with varying textures and pops of colour mixed in with the decor.\nL24: Given that our kitchen is on the smaller side with limited counter space, we have to be very selective about what stays out at any given time. So, when it came time to replace our toaster and tea kettle, both needed to be hard-working, sleek and stylish. Of course, I immediately turned to my go-to brand, Breville.\nL25: ## Breville Luxe Collection\nL26: \nL27: cite12†Image: Breville Damson Blue Toaster and Kettle in White Kitchen L28: \nL29: Some links used in this post are affiliates. Please refer to my cite13†disclosure policy for more information.\nL30: \nL31: Gorgeous small appliances, right?\nL32: I’m sure you’re not surprised by the rich, deep shade of blue I selected called cite14†Damson Blue†www.breville.com . Not only is it on trend with Pantone’s Colour of the Year, Classic Blue, it’s also one of my favourites for its ability to make a statement, yet remain timeless. I’d love to see this lovely hue in a kitchen with wood or grey cabinets too. So beautiful!\nL33: \nL34: cite15†Image: Breville Blue Kettle in White Kitchen with Coffee Cup and Donuts L35: Breville’s Luxe Collection includes other luxurious colours like Black Truffle, Sea Salt, Royal Champagne and more, making it easy to coordinate with any kitchen.\nL36: \nL37: If you’re wanting to test colours and visualize placement in your own kitchen, there’s an augmented reality app you can download (cite16†Apple Store†apps.apple.com or cite17†Google Play†play.google.com ) to provide a 360° experience. So helpful and fun, right? You really can’t go wrong with any of the metallic finishes paired with chrome accents!\nL38: cite18†Image: Breville Damson Blue Smart Kettle on White Kitchen Counter with French Press Coffee L39: \nL40: I had the kettle and toaster unboxed and ready to go in less than 5 minutes. I think you’d be hard-pressed to find a quicker way to modernize a kitchen. Gorgeous small kitchen appliances like these make a dramatic difference with very little effort.\nL41: \nL42: Now, let’s take a closer look at some of my favourite features of our new toaster and tea kettle…\nL43: ## The Smart Kettle™ Luxe\nL44: \nL45: Do you start your morning with coffee or tea? If someone could hand me a cup the minute I wake up, I’d be one happy girl! Of course, I love using our cite19†Breville coffee maker when making multiple cups. But, when I’m by myself, French press is quick, easy and satisfying.\nL46: \nL47: cite20†Image: Making French Press Coffee with Breville's Smart Kettle in Damson Blue L48: No matter what I’m brewing, coffee or different types of tea (black, green, white or oolong), the smart kettle knows the ideal temperature to bring out optimal taste and quality with the simple press of a button. Effortless, right?! So helpful, especially in the morning when my brain is still a bit foggy!\nL49: \nL50: cite21†Image: Breville Smart Kettle Luxe Variable Temperature Settings L51: Of course, safety features are important when we’re talking about hot water. The soft opening lid, clear view dual windows and auto shut off so the kettle won’t boil dry give me peace of mind. I love that it’s made with BPA free materials too. The list goes on and on…\nL52: \nL53: cite22†Image: Breville Smart Kettle Luxe with Soft Opening Lid and Clear View Windows L54: \nL55: Don’t let its good looks fool you. This cite23†kettle†www.breville.com is packed full of straightforward features that make life simpler.\nL56: ## The Toast Select™ Luxe\nL57: \nL58: As with most families, toast (or some version of) is a morning staple around here. And, on days when we have leftover cite24†waffles , our toaster is what we use to heat them up. To say it gets used A LOT is an understatement.\nL59: \nL60: cite25†Image: Making Toast with Blue Toaster in White Kitchen --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSmall Kitchen Appliances You'll Use and Love (I Do!) - Satori Design for Living (https://satoridesignforliving.com/small-kitchen-appliances-youll-use-and-love-i-do/)\nciteturn4view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn2view0\",\"lineno\":60}); Total lines: 110\nL35: Breville’s Luxe Collection includes other luxurious colours like Black Truffle, Sea Salt, Royal Champagne and more, making it easy to coordinate with any kitchen.\nL36: \nL37: If you’re wanting to test colours and visualize placement in your own kitchen, there’s an augmented reality app you can download (cite16†Apple Store†apps.apple.com or cite17†Google Play†play.google.com ) to provide a 360° experience. So helpful and fun, right? You really can’t go wrong with any of the metallic finishes paired with chrome accents!\nL38: cite18†Image: Breville Damson Blue Smart Kettle on White Kitchen Counter with French Press Coffee L39: \nL40: I had the kettle and toaster unboxed and ready to go in less than 5 minutes. I think you’d be hard-pressed to find a quicker way to modernize a kitchen. Gorgeous small kitchen appliances like these make a dramatic difference with very little effort.\nL41: \nL42: Now, let’s take a closer look at some of my favourite features of our new toaster and tea kettle…\nL43: ## The Smart Kettle™ Luxe\nL44: \nL45: Do you start your morning with coffee or tea? If someone could hand me a cup the minute I wake up, I’d be one happy girl! Of course, I love using our cite19†Breville coffee maker when making multiple cups. But, when I’m by myself, French press is quick, easy and satisfying.\nL46: \nL47: cite20†Image: Making French Press Coffee with Breville's Smart Kettle in Damson Blue L48: No matter what I’m brewing, coffee or different types of tea (black, green, white or oolong), the smart kettle knows the ideal temperature to bring out optimal taste and quality with the simple press of a button. Effortless, right?! So helpful, especially in the morning when my brain is still a bit foggy!\nL49: \nL50: cite21†Image: Breville Smart Kettle Luxe Variable Temperature Settings L51: Of course, safety features are important when we’re talking about hot water. The soft opening lid, clear view dual windows and auto shut off so the kettle won’t boil dry give me peace of mind. I love that it’s made with BPA free materials too. The list goes on and on…\nL52: \nL53: cite22†Image: Breville Smart Kettle Luxe with Soft Opening Lid and Clear View Windows L54: \nL55: Don’t let its good looks fool you. This cite23†kettle†www.breville.com is packed full of straightforward features that make life simpler.\nL56: ## The Toast Select™ Luxe\nL57: \nL58: As with most families, toast (or some version of) is a morning staple around here. And, on days when we have leftover cite24†waffles , our toaster is what we use to heat them up. To say it gets used A LOT is an understatement.\nL59: \nL60: cite25†Image: Making Toast with Blue Toaster in White Kitchen L61: I’m sure you can see why I appreciate the cite26†luxe toaster’s variable settings†www.breville.com that automatically adjust the toasting time for different types of bread. Whole wheat, white, bagels, waffles, pastries or english muffins- it does them all. And just look at that LED progress indicator that counts down. Brilliant!\nL62: And, because we all like it toasted a bit different around here (light to dark), the lift and look handle and ‘A Bit More’ button are both fantastic. It easily handles frozen bread too.\nL63: \nL64: cite27†Image: Breville 2-Slice Luxe Toaster in Damson Blue on White Countertop L65: \nL66: Just look at those extra wide and deep slots. No more bagels getting stuck or having to turn them around to brown all sides. Speaking from experience, I think we all could use a few more trouble-free mornings, right?!\nL67: cite28†Image: Breville Blue Toaster with Strawberry Cream Cheese Toast L68: \nL69: Probably what I love most about this ultimate 2-slice toaster is how its vibrant look and user-friendliness have inspired me to create colourful and fresh new recipes like this cite29†strawberry cream cheese toast cite30†.†www.instagram.com What would you make with yours?\nL70: \nL71: Shop this Post\nL72: \nL73: cite31†Image†assets.rewardstyle.com JavaScript is currently disabled in this browser. Reactivate it to view this content.\nL74: ## More Breville Kitchen Appliance Reviews\nL75: \nL76:   * cite19†Connecting Over Coffee with Breville L77:   * cite32†Lavender London Fog Latte for Mom L78:   * cite24†My Favourite Classic Waffle Recipe L79: \nL80: Enjoy your day!\nL81: \nL82: cite33†Image: Shauna at Satori Design for Living Blog - Home Decor, DIY, Vintage Finds, Recipes L83: \nL84: cite34†Shauna Oberg L85: Hi there, I'm Shauna. I believe the most meaningful homes are built over time, with thoughtful choices, personal touches, and a mix of things you love. I share decorating ideas, DIY projects, renovation lessons, and seasonal inspiration to help you shape a home that feels collected, welcoming, and reflective of the way you live... cite35†Read More L86: \nL87: cite36†Previous Where I’m at in My Health Journey One Year Later L88: \nL89: cite37†Next Creamy Pumpkin Spice Latte (with Real Pumpkin) L90: Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *\nL91: \nL92: Comment *\nL93: \nL94: [Input: John Doe]Name *\nL95: \nL96: [Input: john@example.com]Email *\nL97: \nL98: [Input: https://www.example.com]Website\nL99: \nL100: Rating Rating [Input]\nL101: [Input]\nL102: [Input]\nL103: [Input]\nL104: [Input]\nL105: [Input]\nL106: \nL107: [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL108: \nL109: [Input]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKitchen Remodel Final Reveal - Design Dazzle (https://www.designdazzle.com/kitchen-remodel-final-reveal/)\nciteturn4view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 9 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn2view1\",\"lineno\":80}); Total lines: 486\nL25:   * cite0†Home L26:   * cite1†Home Decor / Design L27:   * cite2†Holidays L28:   * cite3†Crafts L29:   * cite4†All Categories L30: \nL31: *   * cite5†Facebook†www.facebook.com L32:   * cite6†Instagram†www.instagram.com L33:   * cite7†Pinterest†www.pinterest.com L34:   * cite8†YouTube†www.youtube.com L35: \nL36: ×\nL37: \nL38: cite0†Design Dazzle » cite9†My Projects L39: \nL40: Published: Nov 9, 2016 · Modified: Aug 3, 2022 by cite10†Toni Roberts · This post may contain affiliate links · cite11†33 Comments L41: # Kitchen Remodel Final Reveal\nL42: \nL43: I am so excited to finally share the final installment of my kitchen remodel with you: The reveal!\nL44: \nL45: It’s been so fun to share each step of the process with you, and I absolutely love the way that everything has come together and turned out. I love, love, LOVE my kitchen now. It’s perfectly suited to my needs and style. Cooking, entertaining, and just hanging out are infinitely more enjoyable! And what really important factor – it makes me want to cook in there!\nL46: As a reminder, here’s a little bit of what my kitchen cite12†looked like before: L47: \nL48: cite75†Image: kitchen before-7-2 L49: \nL50: And here’s what it looks like now!\nL51: \nL52: cite76†Image: Make sure to check out the before pictures for my Kitchen Remodel | Design Dazzle L53: \nL54: cite77†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L55: \nL56: It’s been such an amazing transformation process! All the time and effort has been completely worth it, but I have to say, I’m so glad it’s finally done!\nL57: \nL58: cite78†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L59: cite79†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L60: \nL61: cite80†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L62: \nL63: cite81†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L64: \nL65: We had a cabinet maker take care of all the custom work, and it turned out beautifully!\nL66: \nL67: After the cabinets came the paint. I decided on two Benjamin Moore colors.cite13† Edgecomb Gray†www.benjaminmoore.com for the walls, and cite14†White Dove†www.benjaminmoore.com for the cabinets and crown molding. The colors complement each other so well!\nL68: For the cite15†countertops , I decided that Viatera quartz would be the best option. I paired it with a beautiful, classic white subway tile. I love my countertops!\nL69: \nL70: cite82†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L71: \nL72: cite83†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L73: \nL74: cite84†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L75: cite16†Farmhouse sinks†www.homedepot.com are my favorite and there’s no way I was going to choose anything else! It looks beautiful with the countertops since the clean lines don’t distract from anything!\nL76: \nL77: cite85†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L78: \nL79: cite86†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L80: \nL81: cite87†Image: Kitchen Remodel Reveal | Design Dazzle L82: I love that I’m able to hide away all the counter clutter and use the kitchen as another place to decorate and style. If there’s going to be anything on my counter that people are going to see, I want it to be pretty!\nL83: \nL84: It’s been such a pleasure to show you all the steps and the process of my remodel! I hope that it’s inspired you to take on the challenge of renovating a room, and maybe given you some tips and ideas, too!\nL85: ## Check out the rest of my kitchen remodel!\nL86: \nL87: #### cite12†Kitchen Remodel: Before L88: \nL89: #### cite17†Kitchen Remodel: During L90: \nL91: #### cite18†Slide-Out Kitchen Shelves L92: \nL93: #### cite19†Kitchen Cabinet Surprise  L94: \nL95: #### cite20†At Home Baking Zone L96: \nL97: #### cite21†Kitchen Knife Drawer L98: \nL99: #### cite15†Countertops and Tile L100: \nL101: #### cite22†Hidden Kitchen TV L102: \nL103: #### cite23†Creative Kitchen Storage Solutions L104: \nL105: #### cite24†Kitchen Finishing Touches L106: #### Final Reveal (The post you’re reading now)\nL107: \nL108: Check out some of the other cite25†One Room Challenge from Calling It Home!†www.callingithome.com L109: \nL110: cite88†Image: signature_toni.jpg L111: \nL112: Save\nL113: \nL114: Save\nL115: \nL116: Save\nL117: \nL118: Save\nL119: \nL120: cite89†Image: LOVE my kitchen now. It’s perfectly suited to my needs and style. Cooking, entertaining, and just hanging out are infinitely more enjoyable! And what really important factor – it makes me want to cook in there! L121: ## More My Projects\nL122: \nL123:   * cite26†Christmas Tree Decorating Tips & Hacks L124:   * cite27†Home Gym Accent Wall L125:   * cite28†Best Man Cave Bathroom Ideas Vintage Auto Shop Theme L126:   * cite29†Baking Zone Organization And Kitchen Supplies Storage L127: \nL128: Sharing is caring!\nL129: \nL130:   * cite30† †www.facebook.com L131:   *\nL132: \nL133: ## Reader Interactions\nL134: ### Comments\nL135: \nL136:   1.\nL137: \nL138: Darlene says\nL139: \nL140: November 10, 2016 at 7:48 am\nL141: \nL142: WOW, now this is a big change. Well done – it’s so bright and cheery! I especially like that you added your own personality with the turquoise pieces and the adorable stool covers\nL143: \nL144: Darlene\nL145: cite31†http://www.BundleMeBaby.etsy.com†www.BundleMeBaby.etsy.com L146: \nL147: cite32†Reply L148: \nL149:      *\nL150: \nL151: Toni - Design Dazzle says\nL152: \nL153: November 15, 2016 at 1:40 pm\nL154: \nL155: Thank you Darlene! I couldn’t wait to add my style to the kitchen. I’m loving it!\nL156: Toni\nL157: \nL158: cite33†Reply L159:   2.\nL160: \nL161: Jen @ Noting Grace says\nL162: \nL163: November 10, 2016 at 9:58 am\nL164: \nL165: Toni! What an amazing transformation! You completely knocked this one out of the park!! Brava!!!\nL166: \nL167: I bet you were so happy to see those awkward swivel chairs go! You’ve brought this kitchen up to date with gorgeous results! Congratulations!\nL168: \nL169: cite34†Reply L170: \nL171:      *\nL172: \nL173: Toni - Design Dazzle says\nL174: \nL175: November 15, 2016 at 1:36 pm\nL176: \nL177: Yes, Jen so happy to see those swivel chair go! LOL I appreciate your sweet comments. It was a fun remodel.\nL178: Toni\nL179: cite35†Reply L180: \nL181:   3.\nL182: \nL183: Cassie Bustamante says\nL184: \nL185: November 10, 2016 at 11:39 am\nL186: \nL187: what a difference! so fresh and bright- love the touches of aqua!\nL188: \nL189: cite36†Reply L190: \nL191:      *\nL192: \nL193: Toni - Design Dazzle says\nL194: \nL195: November 11, 2016 at 8:54 am\nL196: \nL197: Thank you Cassie! I love cooking in my kitchen. I’ll be changing out the touches of aqua at Christmas. The aqua is my spring/summer decor. Not much to change out.\nL198: \nL199: cite37†Reply L200: \nL201:   4.\nL202: \nL203: lauren | love lola says\nL204: \nL205: November 10, 2016 at 1:58 pm\nL206: I cannot believe you pulled this off in only five weeks. It is beautiful and perfect!!\nL207: \nL208: cite38†Reply L209: \nL210:      *\nL211: \nL212: Toni - Design Dazzle says\nL213: \nL214: November 15, 2016 at 1:37 pm\nL215: \nL216: Thank you, Lauren! It actually took me about 6-7 weeks of construction – with a few weeks of planning and getting bids. I’ve done a few kitchens. This is my favorite.\nL217: Toni\nL218: \nL219: cite39†Reply L220: \nL221:   5.\nL222: \nL223: Krista says\nL224: \nL225: November 10, 2016 at 3:51 pm\nL226: \nL227: Um, wow! How unbelievable is this?!? I absolutely adore your kitchen!! Gorgeous choices all around!\nL228: cite40†Reply L229: \nL230:      *\nL231: \nL232: Toni - Design Dazzle says\nL233: \nL234: November 15, 2016 at 1:35 pm\nL235: \nL236: Krista – thank you for your kind comments. I’m so enjoying this kitchen!\nL237: \nL238: cite41†Reply L239: \nL240:   6.\nL241: \nL242: Stacey Keeling says\nL243: \nL244: November 10, 2016 at 5:50 pm\nL245: \nL246: Absolutely beautiful!!\nL247: \nL248: cite42†Reply L249: \nL250:      *\nL251: \nL252: Toni - Design Dazzle says\nL253: \nL254: November 15, 2016 at 1:34 pm\nL255: \nL256: Thank you Stacey. I really love my kitchen!\nL257: \nL258: cite43†Reply L259: \nL260:      *\nL261: \nL262: Toni - Design Dazzle says\nL263: \nL264: November 15, 2016 at 1:38 pm\nL265: Stacey – It brings a smile on my face when I walk in and see my kitchen – remodeled, clean and with decor I love.\nL266: Thank you!\nL267: Toni\nL268: \nL269: cite44†Reply L270: \nL271:   7.\nL272: \nL273: Iris Nacole says\nL274: \nL275: November 13, 2016 at 7:19 am\nL276: \nL277: This is such a dreamy makeover! I love what paint can do to a space, and in here, it’s made this entire room inviting, and eye-catching. Enjoy it all!\nL278: \nL279: cite45†Reply L280: \nL281:   8.\nL282: \nL283: Andi says\nL284: \nL285: November 14, 2016 at 9:28 am\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKitchen Tour - ZDesign At Home (https://www.zdesignathome.com/kitchen-tour/)\nciteturn4view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view2\",\"lineno\":215}); Total lines: 508\nL183: Hi! I’m not crazy about the color, that’s all. You can’t really tell in the photos too much but for me they have a bad gold undertone which can do weird things to the paint color on the walls, if you know what I mean. And yes, they are just like any other wood floor as far as keeping clean. And they are real hard wood…just a type of technology that expands and contracts over time so that it won’t creek. Other than that they are fine and wear well. Hope that helps and thanks for stopping by!! 🙂\nL184:   5. cite85†Image†secure.gravatar.com Susan cowart says:\nL185: \nL186: cite86†March 12, 2016 at 4:34 am L187: \nL188: Can you give source for the pantry door? If not, size?\nL189: \nL190:     1. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL191: \nL192: cite87†March 15, 2016 at 10:33 pm L193: \nL194: Hi Susan, The pantry door is 32′ W x 8′ H. I do not have the source as we purchased the doors with the house through our builder. I hope that helps and thanks for stopping in!!\nL195: \nL196:   6. cite88†Image†secure.gravatar.com Elaine says:\nL197: \nL198: cite89†March 12, 2016 at 5:00 pm L199: Your kitchen is such a beautiful space! The white is so clean and fresh! I have one question. I live in a builder home, and bit by bit we are tweaking it to make it ours. I noticed that your cabinets are very tall, specifically above the fridge, but also the upper cabinets with glass seem to have more height than many I have seen. I would easily have space to do this in my kitchen, as it is a vaulted ceiling.\nL200: I realize you had mentioned you had not put items in the glass cupboards yet, but how about the other cabinets that are tall, do you find them functional storage? Again the kitchen is just gorgeous, thanks for sharing!\nL201:     1. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL202: \nL203: cite90†March 15, 2016 at 10:27 pm L204: \nL205: Hi Elaine! Yes, I have stored stuff in all of the cabinets except for some of the glass ones. They are just as deep and as the others so they provide plenty of storage plus, they make the kitchen look so much prettier. I’m glad we did the uppers because the look, feel, and the extra storage make it the perfect kitchen. I’m so happy you like it and thank you so much for stopping by and for commenting!!\nL206:   7. cite91†Image†secure.gravatar.com cite92†Shauna†www.thehouseofsilverlining.com says:\nL207: \nL208: cite93†March 13, 2016 at 5:34 am L209: \nL210: Your kitchen is just so beautiful Bree! And you just may have (big maybe) convinced me to use marble in the next kitchen. Such a good, informative post!\nL211: xoxo\nL212: \nL213:     1. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL214: \nL215: cite94†March 15, 2016 at 10:37 pm L216: Thank you so much, Shauna!! I think you will do fine with marble but like I said in the post, I would use something different on the center island and/or prep area like stainless Steele or butchers block. I do love quartz though and I think both are gorgeous!! Thank you for stopping in and for always being so sweet with your words! Hugs!!\nL217: \nL218:   8. cite95†Image†secure.gravatar.com Debbie says:\nL219: \nL220: cite96†March 17, 2016 at 11:52 am L221: I follow you on IG and just now checked out your blog. Your kitchen is beautiful! I do love the airy-ness and that clean look. We’re a first time home owner and had chosen espresso cabinets for our first home build for that modern feel. I still like it but seeing all your white cabinets leaves me drooling. We did choose white quartz countertops with some crystal specks and that helped make the kitchen look somewhat airy.\nL222: It would drive me nuts if I saw stains or chips on the counter so I’m happy with the quartz. Your storage space is amazing! I would totally buy your house if I could afford it!\nL223:     1. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL224: \nL225: cite97†March 17, 2016 at 3:20 pm L226: \nL227: So glad you like my kitchen and I love the quartz you are talking about as I’ve used it before (recently) for a client. It’s my favorite one of all the quartz options!! I bet your kitchen is gorgeous and thanks again for stopping by:)\nL228: \nL229:   9. cite95†Image†secure.gravatar.com Debbie says:\nL230: \nL231: cite98†March 17, 2016 at 1:02 pm L232: Bree, I forgot to add this to my previous comment. I’m liking the herringbone pattern backsplash in your kitchen. Do you think that would work with espresso colored cabinets and modern style? I wouldn’t want marble material for our backsplash just for ease of maintenance though.\nL233: \nL234:     1. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL235: \nL236: cite99†March 17, 2016 at 3:24 pm L237: It might work, Debbie. It would give the space a bit more of a transitional feel but it would work I think. I would buy a sample first though and compare it to your cabinets and countertops as you would want to make sure it doesn’t clash with the counter tops. If your style is more modern though, I would probably do a glass tile or a subway tile in a color that will blend well with your counter tops. Hope that helps and sorry for all of the reply’s today! Xoxo:)\nL238:   10. Pingback: cite100†Barstools Basics (+ my faves) - ZDesign At Home L239: \nL240:   11. cite74†Image†secure.gravatar.com Corey says:\nL241: \nL242: cite101†March 19, 2016 at 8:27 pm L243: \nL244: Your kitchen is gorgeous! We have looked everywhere for a wooden light, similar to the one over your breakfast table, to balance all the the white and stainless in our kitchen. Do you mind to share the brand or where you found it? Thank you so much!\nL245: \nL246:     1. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL247: \nL248: cite102†March 20, 2016 at 3:11 pm L249: Hi Corey! We got this one at Arhaus years ago and I should have sourced a similar one because this one is no longer available:(…I’m so sorry! However, if you will just google wooden chandelier there are similar ones out there. Not exact but very close (trust me I know because I tried to find an exact match to it when we built the house because I already had this one and I wanted another one so I could put two over the island). Hope that helps some and thanks so much for stopping by the blog:)!!\nL250:     2. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL251: \nL252: cite103†March 20, 2016 at 3:49 pm L253: \nL254: Hi again, Corey! I went ahead and added a couple of very similar style chandelier links at the bottom of my kitchen tour post for you. Hope that helps:)\nL255: \nL256:   12. cite104†Image†secure.gravatar.com cite105†spiderman coloring pages†www.youtube.com says:\nL257: \nL258: cite106†March 24, 2016 at 9:14 pm L259: I was very pleased to find this web-site.I wanted to thanks for your time for this wonderful read!! I definitely enjoying every little bit of it and I have you bookmarked to check out new stuff you blog post.\nL260: \nL261:     1. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL262: \nL263: cite107†March 24, 2016 at 10:21 pm L264: \nL265: Hi Earlene! So nice to have you following along and thanks for stopping by the blog! Hope to see you back soon:))\nL266: \nL267:   13. cite108†Image†secure.gravatar.com cite109†eebest8 seo†fiverr.com says:\nL268: cite110†April 4, 2016 at 2:11 am L269: \nL270: Thanks again for the post.Thanks Again. Fantastic.\nL271: \nL272:     1. cite59†Image†secure.gravatar.com zdesign.breehancock says:\nL273: \nL274: cite111†April 5, 2016 at 1:48 pm L275: \nL276: Thank you and thanks for stopping by the blog!!\nL277: \nL278:   14. Pingback: cite26†A Kitchen Backsplash Transformation + A Design Decision Gone Wrong - ZDesign At Home L279: \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTaking Toast to the Next Level With Revolution Cooking - Thou Swell (https://thouswell.com/smart-toaster-toast-recipes-revolution-cooking/)\nciteturn4view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.3 years ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://thouswell.com/smart-toaster-toast-recipes-revolution-cooking/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 156\n"
